@startuml
title Kill during the unit, then resume a run

actor Operator
participant "avarice CLI" as CLI
participant Supervisor
database Ledger
participant "Run clone" as Clone
participant "Claude Code host" as Host
participant "PreToolUse hook" as Hook

== Before the kill ==
Supervisor -> Ledger : item delegated, snapshot step, launch step started (session ID)
note over Ledger : one invocation unit reserved
Supervisor -> Host : launch (detached process group)
Host -> Hook : tool calls
Hook -> Ledger : charge tool calls and subagents
Host -> Clone : edit files
Operator ->x Supervisor : kill (no cleanup)
note over Ledger : run stays running, item stays delegated,\nlaunch row stays started, reservation stays,\nlease stays recorded until it expires
note over Host, Hook : the host keeps running and the hook keeps charging the run budget
note over CLI : status presents the run as paused (supervisor interrupted)\nonce the lease has lapsed; the ledger state is unchanged.\nstart --wait then prints "interrupted" with the resume command, exit 3

== The resume command ==
Operator -> CLI : resume RUN_ID
CLI -> Ledger : read the run
alt stop state, or a state resume does not continue
  CLI --> Operator : report the state, no lease (exit 0 at ready_for_review, else 3)
else lease still live (up to 180 s after the last renewal)
  CLI --> Operator : refused, the lease must expire first (exit 3), nothing changed
else lease free or expired
  CLI -> Ledger : read the latest checkpoint and the open attempt
  CLI --> Operator : resuming from running, interrupted attempt and step
  CLI -> Supervisor : spawn a detached supervisor
  CLI -> Ledger : step supervisor:resume
end

== Prelude under the lease ==
Supervisor -> Ledger : take the lease (fence raised: a late write from the dead holder is refused)
Supervisor -> Ledger : read launch rows left started
Supervisor -> Host : find the process by session ID, end its group
alt the reap fails
  Supervisor -> Ledger : step resume:reconcile failed, every row stays started
  CLI --> Operator : with --wait: could not be resumed (exit 70)
else ended, none found, or the host cannot reap
  Supervisor -> Ledger : warning event if a process was ended
  Supervisor -> Ledger : launch rows marked interrupted, one event per invocation
end
Supervisor -> Ledger : spend the orphaned reservation at its cost cap\n(no wall clock charged, nothing refunded)

== Reconcile the item ==
Supervisor -> Ledger : run running to paused (reason interrupted)
Supervisor -> Clone : read HEAD, compare with the attempt's snapshot
alt HEAD moved under a delegated item
  Supervisor -> Ledger : containment finding, decision record,\nrun blocked_on_decision (enforcement failure), no discard
else the launch step names the attempt (the unit ran)
  Supervisor -> Ledger : classify step: inconclusive (interrupted), unless already classified
  alt the interrupted attempt was already the retry
    Supervisor -> Ledger : decision record (repeated failure), run blocked_on_decision
  else the invocations budget cannot cover another unit
    Supervisor -> Ledger : decision record, run blocked_on_decision (budget exhausted)
  else the one retry is still available
    Supervisor -> Ledger : checkpoint discard-attempt
    Supervisor -> Clone : restore the snapshot (paths the unit changed only)
    Supervisor -> Ledger : discard step, attempt discarded, item delegated to ready
    Supervisor -> Ledger : run paused to running (next: context pack)
  end
else no launch step (killed before the launch)
  Supervisor -> Clone : restore the snapshot when one exists (nothing to undo)
  Supervisor -> Ledger : item back to ready, the retry is not used
  Supervisor -> Ledger : run paused to running
end

== The loop continues ==
Supervisor -> Ledger : a retry attempt is opened, then as in the run to ready flow
note over Supervisor, Ledger : a kill inside the retry blocks the run with a decision\nnaming both attempts and how each ended
@enduml
